Q: Mail Generator with formatting A: <p>Not a dedicated framework, but what you are asking for can basically be done pretty simply by using format strings and Squeak's SMTPClient:</p>
<pre class="lang-none prettyprint-override"><code>&quot;todo: use proper Customer objects here&quot;
customers := #(('ID20302323' 'John' 'Doe' 'john@does.com') ('ID18547659' 'Joanna' 'Doe' 'joanna@does.com')).

messages := customers collect: [:ea |
    MailMessage empty
        setField: 'to' toString: ea fourth;
        setField: 'subject' toString: ('Buy our product, {1}' translated format: {ea second});
        body: (MIMEDocument contentType: MIMEDocument contentTypePlainText content: ('Hi {1} {2},

Please check out https://example.com and send us your money!

Best,
Incorporated' format: {ea second. ea third}));
        yourself].

client := (SMTPClient openOnHostNamed: MailSender smtpServer port: MailSender smtpServerPort)
    user: MailSender userName;
    password: MailSender userPassword;
    login;
    yourself.
messages
    do: [:ea |
        client
            mailFrom: MailSender userEmail
            to: ((ea to findTokens: ',') collect: #withBlanksTrimmed)
            text: ea asSendableText]
    displayingProgress: 'Sending messages...'.
</code></pre>
<p>You can also create rich text messages like this:</p>
<pre class="lang-none prettyprint-override"><code>MIMEDocument newMultipart
    contentTypeHeaderValue: (MIMEHeaderValue fromMIMEHeader: MIMEDocument contentTypeMultipartAlternative);
    addPart: (MIMEDocument contentType: MIMEDocument contentTypePlainText content: ('Hi {1} {2},

Please check out https://example.com and send us your money!

Best,
Incorporated' format: {ea second. ea third}));
    addPart: (MIMEDocument contentType: MIMEDocument contentTypeHtml content: ('&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Hi {1} {2},&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Please check out &lt;a href=&quot;https://example.com&quot;&gt;https://example.com&lt;/a&gt; and send us your money!&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Best,&lt;br&gt;
Incorporated&lt;/p&gt;' format: {ea second escapeEntities. ea third escapeEntities}));
    yourself
</code></pre>

Q: Why the MaxDropDownItems property doesn&#39;t work in C#? A: <p>To be really sure, consider of changing the IntegralHeight to false (default is true) and the ComboBoxStyle to DropDownList (default is DropDown) as well:</p>

<pre><code>ComboBox.IntegralHeight = false;
ComboBox.MaxDropDownItems = 4;
ComboBox.DropDownStyle = ComboBoxStyle.DropDownList;
</code></pre>

<p>This way, you forcefully control your ComboBox display.</p>
